From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:49:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: page hot spots in the 68k template JIT

- in_by_val: `index in array` (the array builtins' hole checks) is true
  for an int32 index below the length of an Int32Shape or
  ContiguousShape array whose element is not a hole.
- get_length and get_by_val on a DirectArguments object (arguments.length
  and arguments[i]) while nothing on it is overridden.
- enumerator_next: for-in's next name while the object keeps the
  enumerator's structure, also on the first step (no indexed
  properties) and the last (the sentinel).
- stricteq and friends: two flat strings with the same StringImpl are
  equal, and two different atoms are not.
- CodeBlock::bytecodeOffset on 68k: the start from the CodeBlock's raw
  instructions pointer, so each slow path's setCurrentVPC calls into
  UnlinkedCodeBlock once instead of three times.

Team 3
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.h    |   9 +
 .../JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp  | 186 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 189 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.h b/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.h
index 80a38217d2c..00da6633dc1 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.h
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/CodeBlock.h
@@ -321,10 +321,19 @@ public:
 
     inline unsigned bytecodeOffset(const JSInstruction* returnAddress)
     {
+#if CPU(M68K)
+        // Every slow path sets the call site from its PC: the start from this
+        // CodeBlock, and one call for the size instead of three.
+        const auto* instructionsBegin = static_cast<const JSInstruction*>(m_instructionsRawPointer);
+        uintptr_t offset = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(returnAddress) - reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(instructionsBegin);
+        RELEASE_ASSERT(offset < instructions().size());
+        return offset;
+#else
         const auto* instructionsBegin = instructions().at(0).ptr();
         const auto* instructionsEnd = reinterpret_cast<const JSInstruction*>(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(instructionsBegin) + instructions().size());
         RELEASE_ASSERT(returnAddress >= instructionsBegin && returnAddress < instructionsEnd);
         return returnAddress - instructionsBegin;
+#endif
     }
 
     inline BytecodeIndex bytecodeIndex(const JSInstruction* returnAddress)
